1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,525
Mister Orrin sold time. Five extra minutes, for one silver coin!

2
00:00:04,925 --> 00:00:08,005
And what about Nora? Nora never had enough of it.

3
00:00:08,305 --> 00:00:12,577
Five more! Quick, please! Spend them wisely, my dear.

4
00:00:13,027 --> 00:00:15,439
The first five, she spent finishing a report.

5
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:18,894
The next five, answering messages. Ping! Ping! Ping!

6
00:00:19,194 --> 00:00:23,523
Soon she was buying them every single day, and filling every one, with more work.

7
00:00:24,073 --> 00:00:27,274
Then one evening, her little boy held up a paper boat.

8
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:29,443
Mum, look! Will you watch it float?

9
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:31,241
In a minute, sweetheart.

10
00:00:31,741 --> 00:00:35,565
She reached for another five. Her purse... was empty.

11
00:00:36,065 --> 00:00:38,365
So she ran! All the way back to the clock shop.

12
00:00:38,645 --> 00:00:40,645
Please! I just need five more minutes!

13
00:00:41,045 --> 00:00:48,139
Oh, my dear. I never made a single minute. I only borrow them from later.

14
00:00:48,689 --> 00:00:53,633
Later? When is later? When he's too big, for paper boats.

15
00:00:54,483 --> 00:00:59,260
Nora looked at the clock. Then at her phone. And she switched it off.

16
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,831
Okay, sweetheart. Show me.

17
00:01:02,381 --> 00:01:04,934
The little boat floated for exactly five minutes.

18
00:01:05,434 --> 00:01:08,921
Those were the only five minutes, she never had to buy.
